1
00:00:00,260 --> 00:00:04,180
Advanced laws of exponents. Power of a power, power

2
00:00:04,180 --> 00:00:07,517
of a product, power of a fraction, and the

3
00:00:07,517 --> 00:00:12,651
zero exponent. First recognise the structure, then choose the law.

4
00:00:13,120 --> 00:00:15,137
In the last video we multiplied powers with the

5
00:00:15,137 --> 00:00:16,802
same base and added the exponents. But look at

6
00:00:16,802 --> 00:00:20,328
this: a to the power m, all raised to

7
00:00:20,328 --> 00:00:23,376
the power n. Should we add the exponents again?

8
00:00:23,376 --> 00:00:28,460
The structure is different, so the rule is different.

9
00:00:28,460 --> 00:00:30,251
First recognise the structure.

10
00:00:30,780 --> 00:00:34,805
Take a small example: two cubed, all squared. The

11
00:00:34,805 --> 00:00:37,510
inner power is three factors of two: one group.

12
00:00:37,510 --> 00:00:42,560
The outer exponent two makes two copies of that

13
00:00:42,560 --> 00:00:45,220
whole group. So there are two groups with three

14
00:00:45,220 --> 00:00:48,752
factors each: six factors altogether. That is two to

15
00:00:48,752 --> 00:00:51,230
the power six, because three times two is six.

16
00:00:51,230 --> 00:00:55,811
So a power raised to another power multiplies the exponents.

17
00:00:56,507 --> 00:01:00,007
Now with letters. A to the power m, all

18
00:01:00,007 --> 00:01:02,920
raised to the power n, means n copies of

19
00:01:02,920 --> 00:01:06,607
a to the power m. That is m plus

20
00:01:06,607 --> 00:01:09,999
m plus m, n times over, which is m

21
00:01:09,999 --> 00:01:13,747
times n factors of a. So the exponents multiply:

22
00:01:13,747 --> 00:01:17,027
a to the power m, all raised to the

23
00:01:17,027 --> 00:01:20,378
power n, is a to the power m n.

24
00:01:21,008 --> 00:01:24,585
Next, a product inside the brackets: two times three,

25
00:01:24,585 --> 00:01:28,228
all to the power four. The outer exponent four

26
00:01:28,228 --> 00:01:31,468
makes four copies of the bracket. Now regroup: all

27
00:01:31,468 --> 00:01:35,673
the twos together, and all the threes together. That

28
00:01:35,673 --> 00:01:38,688
gives two to the power four times three to

29
00:01:38,688 --> 00:01:42,048
the power four. In general, a b all to

30
00:01:42,048 --> 00:01:44,288
the power m is a to the power m

31
00:01:44,288 --> 00:01:49,059
times b to the power m: the exponent reaches every factor.

32
00:01:49,731 --> 00:01:53,331
Fractions work the same way: two fifths, all cubed.

33
00:01:53,331 --> 00:01:58,871
That is two fifths, times two fifths, times two

34
00:01:58,871 --> 00:02:01,907
fifths. The numerators group: two times two times two,

35
00:02:01,907 --> 00:02:06,551
which is two cubed. The denominators group: five times

36
00:02:06,551 --> 00:02:10,118
five times five, which is five cubed. A fraction

37
00:02:10,118 --> 00:02:13,742
inside brackets is powered on the top and on the bottom.

38
00:02:14,384 --> 00:02:17,088
Why is any non-zero number to the power zero

39
00:02:17,088 --> 00:02:20,594
equal to one? Start with a to the power

40
00:02:20,594 --> 00:02:24,644
four over a to the power four. By ordinary

41
00:02:24,644 --> 00:02:28,084
division, anything divided by itself is one. But by

42
00:02:28,084 --> 00:02:31,794
the quotient law the exponents subtract: four minus four

43
00:02:31,794 --> 00:02:34,124
is zero, so it is also a to the

44
00:02:34,124 --> 00:02:37,744
power zero. Both answers describe the same quantity, so

45
00:02:37,744 --> 00:02:41,675
a to the power zero is one, for any non-zero a.

46
00:02:42,171 --> 00:02:45,231
Now look at the four shapes together. A power

47
00:02:45,231 --> 00:02:49,906
raised to another power: multiply the exponents. A product

48
00:02:49,906 --> 00:02:54,271
inside brackets: distribute the power to both factors. A

49
00:02:54,271 --> 00:02:58,038
fraction inside brackets: power the top and the bottom.

50
00:02:58,038 --> 00:03:01,722
And an exponent of zero: the answer is simply one.

51
00:03:02,418 --> 00:03:06,518
Four mistakes to avoid. First: x squared, all cubed,

52
00:03:06,518 --> 00:03:08,534
is x to the power six, not x to

53
00:03:08,534 --> 00:03:14,525
the power five, because the exponents multiply. Second: a

54
00:03:14,525 --> 00:03:18,418
b all cubed is a cubed b cubed, not

55
00:03:18,418 --> 00:03:23,998
a cubed b. Third: a over b, all squared,

56
00:03:23,998 --> 00:03:27,807
is a squared over b squared. And fourth: seven

57
00:03:27,807 --> 00:03:30,689
to the power zero is one, not zero.

58
00:03:31,302 --> 00:03:34,862
Your turn. Four questions, one for each law. Simplify

59
00:03:34,862 --> 00:03:38,618
three to the power four, all squared. Simplify five

60
00:03:38,618 --> 00:03:42,802
x, all cubed. Simplify three sevenths, all squared. And

61
00:03:42,802 --> 00:03:47,273
work out minus six, all to the power zero.

62
00:03:58,473 --> 00:04:01,769
Three to the power four, all squared, multiplies the

63
00:04:01,769 --> 00:04:05,743
exponents: three to the power eight. Five x, all

64
00:04:05,743 --> 00:04:09,763
cubed, is five cubed x cubed: one hundred and

65
00:04:09,763 --> 00:04:13,833
twenty five x cubed. Three sevenths squared is three

66
00:04:13,833 --> 00:04:17,519
squared over seven squared, that is nine over forty

67
00:04:17,519 --> 00:04:21,204
nine. And minus six to the power zero is one.

68
00:04:21,806 --> 00:04:24,282
One last look. A power of a power multiplies

69
00:04:24,282 --> 00:04:27,531
the exponents. A power of a product distributes to

70
00:04:27,531 --> 00:04:31,326
every factor. A power of a fraction powers the

71
00:04:31,326 --> 00:04:34,736
top and the bottom. And any non-zero base to

72
00:04:34,736 --> 00:04:37,556
the power zero is one. See the structure, then

73
00:04:37,556 --> 00:04:40,071
choose the law. Thank you for watching, and see

74
00:04:40,071 --> 00:04:41,397
you in the next lesson.
